too, and this in defense.

255
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:56,120
My mistake.

256
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:57,991
Just forget what you saw.

257
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:01,928
Anyhow, as I was saying, I'll
play this card in defense mode.

258
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:04,560
Whatever that was, it sure looked ugly.

259
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:05,860
But not metal.

260
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:08,661
Tristan's right.

261
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:10,608
That card wasn't a machine.

262
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:16,180
It was a shadow monster called Zoa, A
beast my Flame Swordsman could post easily.

263
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:20,820
And unlike Machine Monsters,
it's totally vulnerable to magic.

264
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:24,800
Yeah, check out Joey's
big grin. Something's up.

265
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:27,140
I don't know. Huh? Know what?

266
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,540
Go, Flame Swordsman!

267
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:30,620
In attack mode!

268
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:34,980
The attack points of that
Zoa card Keith dropped.

269
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:37,162
They're higher than its defense.

270
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:38,480
So what?

271
00:14:38,860 --> 00:14:40,020
Oh, I see.

272
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:42,297
And I'll add this magic card, too.

273
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:44,968
Since Zoa's attack is
more than his defense,

274
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:48,097
it makes little sense to
play him in defensive mode.

275
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:51,580
Unless Keith is trying to
lure Joey into attacking him.

276
00:14:51,780 --> 00:14:53,080
Go, Salamandra!

277
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:56,420
His magic raises my attack
power by 700 points!

278
00:14:56,660 --> 00:14:59,307
So then Keith must have
shown Zoa on purpose!

279
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:00,560
Joey, wait!

280
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:02,140
Swordsman, attack!

281
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:04,997
I gotcha!

282
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,840
My trap activates! What?

283
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,277
Go, magic metal force!

284
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:14,580
Now Zoha is Metal Zoha, with 400
attack and defense points stronger.

285
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:16,220
Nah, no big thing.

286
00:15:16,460 --> 00:15:18,380
But that's not all, Blondie.

287
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:21,597
That new metallic paint
job he's sporting deflects

288
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:24,337
all magic attacks back
to where they came from.

289
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:25,380
My swordsman!

290
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:26,860
That's right.

291
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:28,100
Just watch this!

292
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:30,630
No!

293
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:43,761
My swordsman's been outmaneuving.

294
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:48,917
You should have seen the look
on your loser face, you dweeb.

295
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:52,706
When your swordsman's own attack
toasted him, it was priceless.

296
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:57,280
And I'm just getting started.

297
00:15:57,940 --> 00:15:58,770
Say, what?

298
00:15:59,140 --> 00:15:59,970
That's right.

299
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:03,177
Next on my list is that
little defense card of yours.

300
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:05,580
But he won't be defending much longer.

301
00:16:05,780 --> 00:16:07,337
A stock defense card?

302
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:09,500
Let's see what you're hiding there.

303
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:13,180
An Axe Raider, huh?

304
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:14,440
No problem.

305
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:16,566
Not for my Metal Zoa, anyway.

306
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:18,120
Oh, no!

307
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:22,157
Joey's life points will be all gone
if that Metal Zoa's attack hits!

308
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:23,240
Ain't tough, bud!

309
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:24,800
Sayonara, sucker!

310
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:27,700
Metal Zoa, attack the Axe Raider!

311
00:16:32,980 --> 00:16:33,880
Where'd he go?

312
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:36,940
Of course!

313
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:38,880
Nice move, huh?

314
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:40,690
All right!

315
00:16:40,773 --> 00:16:43,620
You fell right in my
trap, just like I planned!

316
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:45,010
No way!

317
00:16:45,093 --> 00:16:47,160
You set a trap for me? Perfect!

318
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,831
The Chasm of Spikes card!

319
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,278
Now not only is Metal Zoa destroyed,

320
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:56,087
but one quarter of his attack points will
be deducted from Keith's life points!

321
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,080
Not bad, huh?

322
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:01,477
I only wish you could
have seen the look on your

323
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:04,501
face when that Metal Zoa
of yours got shish kebab.

324
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:05,817
It was priceless.

325
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,260
You tell him!

326
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:12,077
It's about time someone gave that bandit
Keith Jerk a taste of his own medicine!

327
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:15,177
That's not the only way he's
turning the tables on Keith.

328
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:19,237
I think Joey might have finally found
the glitch in those machine monsters.

329
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:21,757
Rather than try and beat
them in a direct assault,

330
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:24,134
he's letting his traps do all the work.

331
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:28,380
And now Keith's only winning
by 100 life points. All right!

332
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:31,020
Go, Joe, go! My turn.

333
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:32,977
At first, I'm laying his face down.

334
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:36,600
Oh, and it's a trap card,
so don't bother attacking.

335
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:39,380
Wow, will you just look at him duel?

336
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:42,227
Careful, you haven't
won this duel yet, Joey.

337
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:43,250
You amateur!

338
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:47,997
That's gotta be the lousiest bluff I've
ever heard in my entire dueling career.

339
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:51,668
And next, I'm switching my Axe
Raider back to defensive mode.

340
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:53,961
And throwing this in attack mode.

341
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,160
Go, Garoozies!

342
00:17:56,420 --> 00:17:58,244
Now chug that pendulum machine.

343
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:01,450
Attack!

344
00:18:01,533 --> 00:18:02,920
With Battle Blade Strike!

345
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:08,390
Punk.

346
00:18:08,473 --> 00:18:09,377
Yeah, that's right.

347
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:12,977
Take a permanent vacation at
the scrapyard, you hunk of junk.

348
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:14,320
Now it's my turn!

349
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:15,640
Launch a spider!

350
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:17,460
Demolish Garoozies!

351
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,660
I knew you didn't have another trap card.

352
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:25,200
Wrong again, Keith.

353
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:28,077
You thought I was bluffing and
now you're gonna pay for it.

354
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,140
What's that?

355
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:31,160
Kunai with chain.

356
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:35,520
And once activated, it raises
my attack power 500 points.

357
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:37,200
Attack, Garuzis!

358
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:38,901
Battleaxe crush!

359
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:48,620
All right, it's still close, but Joey
has just won himself a slight lead.

360
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:50,660
I knew he'd make a comeback!

361
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:55,140
Joey's trusting his instincts
and believing in his cards.

362
00:18:55,380 --> 00:18:57,077
He's dueling like a true champion.

363
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,640
Way to go, Joey.

364
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:02,452
If you keep this up, you'll
be dueling Pegasus in no time.

365
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:07,465
I'm not going to let him
make a fool out of me.

366
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:09,900
What's wrong, Mr. Champ?

367
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:13,860
Don't tell me you're losing
your cool to an amateur like me.

368
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:18,690
What the?

369
00:19:18,773 --> 00:19:19,916
What's the big joke?

370
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:22,337
The joke is on you, Blondie.

371
00:19:22,420 --> 00:19:24,717
You're already counting the
tournament's prize money

372
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:27,357
and this duel ain't even
close to being over yet.

373
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:28,270
Oh, yeah?

374
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:31,769
You think your traps
will last you forever?

375
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:34,756
You're gonna run out sooner or later,

376
00:19:34,980 --> 00:19:39,880
and then I'll bring out my bigger machines
and really give our audience a show

377
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:43,682
You're going down you're
sniffling little wannabe

378
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:46,020
Nobody beats bandit key
